Subject: [EXPERIMENT E01] amdgpu explicit sparse unmaps on CachyOS 7.2.8-1

Based on Natalie Vock's 2026-05-29 "Explicit sync for PRT unmaps" series,
patches 1 and 2. Rebased onto the checksum-pinned CachyOS release.
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Local changes: current userq/drm_exec APIs; retain existing empty-list check;
finish update contexts on close/error paths; release the temporary input
fence reference on allocation failure; preserve handle_moved error returns.
Read-only private marker and eligibility counters identify this experiment.
Do not advertise the old proposed upstream DRM minor version on a newer
kernel. The default path remains implicit; opt-in is per GEM_VA operation.

This patch has not been hardware tested. This is a native-only experiment,
not an instruction to enable explicit unmaps in arbitrary applications.

